WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.460
Chapter one located one contribution in the first touch neuron without making it the

2
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:11.120
whole story. If several mice over-react to the same puff, did the same circuit

3
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:17.380
defect cause it? Keep the colour map: gold sensory neuron, teal dorsal horn, blue

4
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.380
brain.

5
00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:22.853
Start at the gold neuron's terminal inside the teal dorsal horn.

6
00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:32.293
In Mecp2 and Gabrb3 models, evidence supported reduced GABA-A-receptor-dependent

7
00:00:32.293 --> 00:00:33.673
presynaptic inhibition.

8
00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:40.353
Receptor-associated puncta fell, afferent-evoked quantal release rose, and dorsal

9
00:00:40.353 --> 00:00:41.453
root potentials shrank.

10
00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:43.867
Reset the pathway.

11
00:00:45.347 --> 00:00:49.927
The Shank3 model did not show that terminal GABRB3 change.

12
00:00:51.327 --> 00:00:56.647
Cultured large sensory neurons instead had reduced Ih and greater excitability.

13
00:00:58.187 --> 00:01:02.907
The Shank3 model therefore reached a similar tactile endpoint through a different

14
00:01:02.907 --> 00:01:03.907
measured defect.

15
00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:09.687
The same tactile endpoint can arise from different defects in these mouse models.

16
00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:18.827
Mecp2 and Gabrb3 models support a reduced presynaptic GABA-A inhibition account.

17
00:01:20.087 --> 00:01:25.707
The Shank3 model instead showed reduced Ih and greater sensory-neuron excitability.

18
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.240
Mechanism is only one axis.

19
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:35.860
Slide a timeline beneath four mouse-model lanes, from postnatal day four to adult

20
00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:40.520
testing. Every lane later shows a tactile abnormality.

21
00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:46.480
Must every adult tactile phenotype already be present at postnatal day four?

22
00:01:52.433 --> 00:02:00.513
No. Gabrb3 and Mecp2 loss-of-function pups were already more reactive at P4.

23
00:02:00.513 --> 00:02:06.773
Nlgn2 and Rorb mutants were not, although both showed tactile abnormalities as

24
00:02:06.773 --> 00:02:13.633
adults. Two sampled ages separate early from later onset, but do not identify the

25
00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.633
onset day.

26
00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:18.207
Nlgn2 also changed the locus.

27
00:02:19.547 --> 00:02:24.267
Deleting it from dorsal-horn neurons was sufficient for adult tactile alterations.

28
00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:28.867
Emphasise the teal spinal block, not the gold afferent.

29
00:02:30.147 --> 00:02:35.567
Across these models, early reactivity tracked selected later behaviours, but that

30
00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.527
association did not prove causation.

31
00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:43.687
Locus, mechanism and developmental timing must be tested separately.

32
00:02:45.027 --> 00:02:47.587
A shared mouse movement cannot choose among them.

33
00:02:48.827 --> 00:02:51.967
Conditional genetics locates a sufficient contribution.

34
00:02:53.427 --> 00:02:54.987
Physiology tests a mechanism.

35
00:02:56.447 --> 00:03:01.607
Measurements at different ages map a schedule without turning association into a

36
00:03:01.607 --> 00:03:02.887
human developmental rule.

37
00:03:03.967 --> 00:03:07.147
The map explains why one endpoint cannot name its cause.

38
00:03:08.427 --> 00:03:13.127
It does not turn air-puff movement into perception, or mouse development into a

39
00:03:13.127 --> 00:03:18.087
human window. Those translation questions need their own measurements.
